  "id": "eudaimonic-well-being",
  "term": "eudaimonic well-being",
  "definition": "Eudaimonic well-being is a form of well-being concerned with how well a person is functioning and how fully they are realizing their potential. It is considered distinct from subjective well-being, which focuses more on life satisfaction and positive or negative feelings.",
